1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:06,280
Nine when you're setting goals don't be so fixated on the end focus on the journey in front of you.
第九点：设定目标时，不要一味盯着终点；把注意力放在眼前的旅程上。

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:12,040
If you don't you are going to miss out on so many of the opportunities that you could have taken advantage of along the way.
如果不这样，你会错过许多原本可以在途中把握的机会。

3
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:19,079
But you missed out on because you were so tunnel visioned on having to be a particular version of yourself in a particular place having particular things.
但你错过了，因为你太过专注于必须成为某种特定的自己、处于特定的位置、拥有特定的东西。

4
00:00:19,079 --> 00:00:24,760
If you are inevitably going to have the job the belonging the house the travel opportunity whatever you're desiring.
如果你最终会得到那份工作、那种归属、那所房子、那个旅行机会，或任何你渴望的东西。

5
00:00:24,760 --> 00:00:29,000
Why not take a look around at where you are at every single step of the journey to getting there.
那么，在前往目标的每一步，为什么不看看自己此刻所在的地方呢？

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,800
Cuz the journey is never going to come back once you have it you're not going to move backwards.
因为这个过程不会再来一遍；一旦你得到了目标中的东西，就不会往回走。

7
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:37,719
You're not going to be in this particular phase of your life with these people in these places with this mindset working on these particular things.
你不会再次处于人生这个特定的阶段，和这些人一起、在这些地方、带着这样的心态、忙着这些具体的事情。

8
00:00:37,719 --> 00:00:42,600
Enjoy them soak them up there's so much to learn and maybe it will send you on a side quest.
享受这些，充分感受这些；有那么多东西可以学，也许它会带你走上一段支线探索。

9
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:46,120
Maybe it will teach you a few things but you're still always inevitably going to get the end goal.
也许它会教会你一些事，但作者说，你依然最终会到达那个目标。

10
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:51,800
Because honestly one of the hardest lessons I ever learned and this was at 23 was the concept of arrival fallacy.
因为说实话，我学到的最难的一课之一——那时我二十三岁——就是所谓的“到达谬误”。

11
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:57,240
Which is simply the concept of believing that you're going to be happy and content when you finally achieve the thing.
简单来说，这就是相信：当你终于实现那件事时，你就会快乐、满足。

12
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:02,839
But spoiler alert you won't because a thing an achievement an award can't give you happiness.
但提前揭晓一下：作者说，你不会，因为一个东西、一项成就或一个奖项，并不能给你幸福。

13
00:01:02,839 --> 00:01:07,390
A person can't give you happiness only you can only the experience of living life is happiness.
一个人也不能给你幸福，只有你自己可以；按她的说法，唯有生活本身的体验才是幸福。

14
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:11,560
It's the pursuit of happiness it's going on the journey not the destination.
那是追求幸福，是踏上旅程，而不是抵达终点。

15
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:15,959
Reaching the destination that lasts 2 seconds it lasts a day the happiness and the next day you're like well now what.
抵达终点，那只持续两秒；那份快乐持续一天，第二天你就会想：好了，那接下来呢？

16
00:01:15,959 --> 00:01:24,199
Why because that's the way that human beings are wired no achievement in this life can give you happiness because the entire point of this life is to live it.
为什么？因为她认为，人就是这样运作的；人生没有哪项成就能给你幸福，因为人生的全部意义就是去生活。

17
00:01:24,199 --> 00:01:27,160
It's to go on the journey is to explore is to learn the lessons along the way.
就是踏上旅程、探索，并学会沿途的那些功课。

18
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:30,920
And that's why every single time you see a successful person have a business or acquire wealth.
她说，这也就是为什么，每当你看到一个成功人士拥有事业或获得财富。

19
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:34,680
They sell it and then they start again because that's what life is actually about.
他们会把它卖掉，然后重新开始，因为她认为，这才是生活真正的意义。

20
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:39,320
While it is so amazing to celebrate your accomplishments please don't think that that's what life is about.
庆祝自己的成就当然非常美好，但请不要以为人生的意义就是这些。

21
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:47,000
Because the destination make up 2 of what life is 98 of it is who you become on the journey to achieving those things.
因为她说，终点只占人生的百分之二，百分之九十八在于你在实现那些目标的过程中成为了怎样的人。

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,079
And finally 10 the most important one let go of your parents desires and expectations.
最后，第十点，也是最重要的一点：放下父母对你的愿望与期待。

23
00:01:53,079 --> 00:01:59,480
Now disclaimer I am not saying that this is some excuse to disrespect your parents and never take their opinion into account okay.
先声明一下，我不是说这能成为不尊重父母、从不考虑他们意见的借口，好吧。

24
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:05,719
Your parents want the best for you your parents are trying to look after you your parents simply want to protect you and they want to make sure that you're good okay.
父母希望你过得最好，想照顾你，只是想保护你，确保你一切都好。

25
00:02:05,719 --> 00:02:12,680
I'm not telling anybody to stop listening to their parents however this is what I'm saying your parents are playing an old game in a new world.
我并不是叫任何人不要听父母的话；不过，我想说的是，父母是在一个新世界里沿用旧的游戏规则。

26
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:22,920
They are always simply going to see in the lens of their survival journey their generational wounds their trauma their lessons their conditioning.
他们总会从自己的生存历程、代际创伤、自己经历的创伤、经验教训以及受到的熏陶，去看待事情。

27
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:32,670
And most importantly their lived experience don't allow their lived experience to influence the life that you are supposed to experience on your own through your own decision m.
而最重要的是，他们亲身走过的人生。不要让他们的经历左右你本该通过自己的决定、独自体验的人生。

28
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:36,839
Just because they love you doesn't mean they always know what's best for you.
仅仅因为他们爱你，并不意味着他们总是知道什么对你最好。

29
00:02:36,839 --> 00:02:41,640
So please please don't throw away your talents and your choices and your passions.
所以请你、请你不要放弃自己的天赋、选择和热情。

30
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:47,800
Because you think that simply because somebody's older than you and simply because they're telling you what to do means that they are going to be correct about everything.
不要因为有人比你年长、又告诉你该怎么做，就以为他们对所有事情都会判断正确。

31
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:55,640
Because we have seen so many amazing people and artists thrive because they decided to believe in themselves more than what anybody else was telling them.
因为我们见过很多出色的人和艺术家蓬勃发展，正是因为他们决定更多地相信自己，而不是别人告诉他们的话。

32
00:02:55,640 --> 00:03:02,600
And I could have so easily been the type of person that followed a traditional career path because that's what my family was telling me to do.
而我本来也很容易成为那种走传统职业道路的人，因为那就是家人当时叫我做的事。

33
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:06,040
They didn't know what social media was going to lead me to of course they didn't.
他们不知道社交媒体会把我带向哪里，当然，他们并不知道。

34
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:10,520
So I don't even blame them for trying to talk me out of it because they didn't live in that kind of world.
所以，我甚至不怪他们试图说服我放弃，因为他们没有生活在那样的世界里。

35
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:14,440
Now that I'm successful of it they love it they brag about me to their friends.
现在，我靠这件事取得了成功，他们很喜欢，还会向朋友夸耀我。

36
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:20,000
The same people that didn't even want me to do it so please remember that you are here to break cycles not repeat them.
这些人，当初甚至不想让我做这件事。所以请记住：你来到这里，是为了打破循环，而不是重复它们。
